Read thermodynamics and heat transfer from zero (@th-reading: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer, #source "../../electromagnetism/sources/University-Physics-Volume-2.lingua#r_5JQ0CPQ0RNJNVH175Y9V305J5Q", #source "../sources/Introduction-to-Engineering-Thermodynamics-Yan.lingua#r_6AX93SRMGE0XXJTQ1NW6X9QXTW", #source "../sources/Engineering-Thermodynamics-Cleynen.lingua#r_38CM7HKS0GSN5T09YDXFKHRVGQ", #thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer "A-thermal-service-and-its-physical-system.lingua#r_13ETYNBXH6JKRVHB3H5KR4QH5Z") { r_4S4VF8JVHQEF1PJ5G3HEQWG8DF
**Read:** [University Physics Volume 2 — OpenStax](../../electromagnetism/sources/University-Physics-Volume-2.lingua#r_5JQ0CPQ0RNJNVH175Y9V305J5Q), chapters 1–4 in full over the introductory sequence; [Introduction to Engineering Thermodynamics — Claire Yu Yan](../sources/Introduction-to-Engineering-Thermodynamics-Yan.lingua#r_6AX93SRMGE0XXJTQ1NW6X9QXTW), the complete six-chapter book with substantial exercises; [Engineering Thermodynamics — Olivier Cleynen](../sources/Engineering-Thermodynamics-Cleynen.lingua#r_38CM7HKS0GSN5T09YDXFKHRVGQ), the entire book as the cycle and entropy sequence develops.

Begin with a cooling drink, a refrigerator, a hot bearing or a furnace. Identify what changes, what crosses a boundary and what must remain within a temperature range. Temperature, stored energy, heat transfer and useful work answer different questions. The early steps build those distinctions without assuming a previous thermodynamics course.

Read all thermal chapters 1–4 of [University Physics Volume 2 — OpenStax](../../electromagnetism/sources/University-Physics-Volume-2.lingua#r_5JQ0CPQ0RNJNVH175Y9V305J5Q) and the complete [Introduction to Engineering Thermodynamics — Claire Yu Yan](../sources/Introduction-to-Engineering-Thermodynamics-Yan.lingua#r_6AX93SRMGE0XXJTQ1NW6X9QXTW) text alongside the introductory steps. Work unfamiliar examples and explain the chosen system before substituting into an equation. Read the whole [Engineering Thermodynamics — Olivier Cleynen](../sources/Engineering-Thermodynamics-Cleynen.lingua#r_38CM7HKS0GSN5T09YDXFKHRVGQ) book through the cycle and second-law development; [Termodinâmica — Bernhard Lesche, UFJF](../sources/Termodinamica-Lesche-UFJF.lingua#r_0ABCKSRZBN8T4Y4FV1FQPWNY4Z) provides a Portuguese companion where its chapters are available. Then study all of [Thermodynamics and Chemistry — Howard DeVoe](../sources/Thermodynamics-and-Chemistry-DeVoe.lingua#r_2YHHGY26Y8X9MS9DB3MXZHD1D1) for the deeper classical and multicomponent foundation.

The complete [A Heat Transfer Textbook — Lienhard and Lienhard](../sources/A-Heat-Transfer-Textbook-Lienhard.lingua#r_7TKQ2D5YRNQ8XVHXNJQDRANWKD) book and [Intermediate Heat and Mass Transfer — MIT 2.51](../sources/Intermediate-Heat-and-Mass-Transfer-MIT-2-51.lingua#r_4NKJ30PDFTY42GJVZX1C2ZS4B8)/[Second Level Course in Heat Transfer — R. P. Vedula](../sources/Second-Level-Heat-Transfer-Vedula.lingua#r_663BY2CF56BBB35C1S595A2VRF) progressions supply heat and mass transfer. Mathematical bridges occur where derivatives, fields, differential equations and numerical methods are used. Later, [Advanced Thermodynamics — MIT 2.43, Spring 2024](../sources/Advanced-Thermodynamics-MIT-2-43.lingua#r_5GXQQ35FEFJM34SWA12X8QHGKC), [Nano-to-Macro Transport Processes — MIT 2.57](../sources/Nano-to-Macro-Transport-MIT-2-57.lingua#r_1YF7TD689ZRGQ51D4B3NGVHZQG) and [Radiative Transfer — MIT 2.58J](../sources/Radiative-Transfer-MIT-2-58J.lingua#r_0SGHEYZJFKN0ZNS3AYJ39XPT86) deepen the foundations and modern transport limits. [Whole books, graduate courses and a sustained thermal programme](../study/Whole-books-graduate-courses-and-a-sustained-thermal-programme.lingua#r_7NHTEAK764F0WSPPZNHZB7CJ1M) joins the substantial reading with advanced practical, numerical and scholarly work. A difficult later stage need not make the first observation difficult.

**Continue:** [A thermal service and its physical system](A-thermal-service-and-its-physical-system.lingua#r_13ETYNBXH6JKRVHB3H5KR4QH5Z).

